From 5fdb64cfde9ac610effb06be3451da8c3c33efcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ja-office-fixes <ja-office-fixes@localhost>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:16:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [de] Set the Latin text of a missing MS Gothic or MS Mincho
 in BIZ UD

MS Gothic and MS Mincho give every Latin letter half the width of a
kanji. When they are not installed, the font picked for them (Arial
Unicode MS on a Mac) is proportional, so lines break elsewhere than in
Word. BIZ UDGothic and BIZ UDMincho have the same widths for every
letter, kana and kanji, so the Latin slots use them when they are
installed. The name shown and saved stays MS Gothic or MS Mincho, and
the East Asian text keeps the font picked as before.
